<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-11T15:00:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump says Russia and Ukraine agree to 'energy ceasefire'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c72be90d017a0c8813dd469cfa64bf786f13838029513516309d67d5897ab5ec</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:59:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T14:39:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261011-trump-says-russia-and-ukraine-agree-energy-ceasefire--acf7a15a4061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-trump-says-russia-and-ukraine-agree-energy-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">US President Trump said Sunday via social media platform Truth Social that Russia and Ukraine had agreed to an energy ceasefire. Neither Kyiv nor Moscow have confirmed their agreement.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: French student protests, October 7 anniversary and Adenot's return to Earth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05e03dc5a86086bc6cfca38651b7536c13964f569ace89341cf749a05d69c049</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:59:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T13:17:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-the-week-in-pictures-french-student-protests-october-7-anniversary-and-adenot-return-to-ear--92c20302aefd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-the-week-in-pictures-french-student-protests-october-7-anniversary-and-adenot-return-to-earth" /><summary type="html">Blockades and protests by French secondary school and university students continued, occasionally becoming violent; French astronaut Sophie Adenot returned to Earth after eight months aboard the International Space Station; Israel's commemorations marking the three-year anniversary of the October 7 attacks: here's a look back at some of the most striking images from the past week's news.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo says will undergo surgery for early-stage lung nodule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec4cb8c1ab7b64a1c9c174cf6d08c78571fa397bc14bc82d704783ff032cbad</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:59:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T10:34:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-pope-leo-says-will-undergo-surgery-for-early-stage-lung-nodule--110af765b1d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-pope-leo-says-will-undergo-surgery-for-early-stage-lung-nodule" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV said Sunday he would undergo surgery in the coming days for a lung nodule detected at an early stage.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says ready to halt refinery strikes if Moscow stops energy attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc47504440a7a052b6152c05d447123664256317cd26f088c1f821db18cf32a6</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T10:21:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-ukraine-ready-halt-refinery-strikes-if-moscow-stops-energy-attacks-zelensky-says--6653602e82d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-ukraine-ready-halt-refinery-strikes-if-moscow-stops-energy-attacks-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Sunday said Kyiv was ready to halt strikes Russian oil refineries if Moscow stopped attacks on Ukrainian energy infrastructure. Zelensky also pushed back on US President Donald Trump's comments made Saturday evening calling for Ukraine to elect a new leader by saying, "It's up to our people".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish PM Sanchez kicks off election campaign amid housing crisis protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca69604a914b4ae59d33aecf78e93c362e5271e01bbec29afe9f0886fb80211c</id><updated>2026-10-11T15:00:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:46:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-spanish-pm-sanchez-kicks-off-election-campaign-amid-housing-crisis-protests--31069b0fb951.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-spanish-pm-sanchez-kicks-off-election-campaign-amid-housing-crisis-protests" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez launched his campaign for a snap November election on Saturday. The vote comes as a deepening housing crisis is driving protests and putting pressure on his left-wing coalition.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Zelensky clash over diesel deal as Russian strikes on Ukraine kill at least 21</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a954a921c6fafdaa8393839816ddff03c8e366572bd7c58b6366779d770e1c6</id><updated>2026-10-11T15:00:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:39:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-trump-zelensky-clash-over-diesel-deal-as-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-kill-21-including-child--ee33fd4d2e87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-trump-zelensky-clash-over-diesel-deal-as-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-kill-21-including-children" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday told reporters that Ukraine should "get a new president", adding that his Ukrainian counterpart Volodymyr Zelensky had disobeyed his orders not to strike Russian refineries. This came after Washington moved to ease sanctions on Russian diesel and as Moscow's strikes on Ukraine, including the city of Zaporizhzhia, killed at least 21 people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says Ukraine needs new president after Zelensky pushes back on diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a36f7e5a978d0b0579465c6303635b240586524fe8628c3efd82a25fc68a5872</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T08:41:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-live-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-zaporizhzhia-kill-least-seven-including-children--2e66a7264c75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-live-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-zaporizhzhia-kill-least-seven-including-children" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday said that Ukraine needs a new president “who can make a deal” to end the war, and called on Ukrainian ‌President Volodymyr ⁠Zelensky to his forces from targeting Russian oil refineries. This came after Washington moved to ease sanctions on Russian diesel and Moscow's continued strikes on Ukraine killed at least 21 people, including four children. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'All human emotions': French astronaut Sophie Adenot returns to Earth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6214af4540776bc5eb66b3c85e4ea62e79e0cbeaac4d5e7579acb8acb94e3958</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T08:09:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-all-human-emotion-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-first-words-since-returning-earth--55457d343553.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-all-human-emotion-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-first-words-since-returning-earth" /><summary type="html">French astronaut Sophie Adenot said she experienced “the full range of human emotions, from the most joyful to the most difficult” during her eight months in space, speaking on Saturday in Cologne, Germany, in her first public appearance since returning to Earth.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>‘So safe you could drink it’: Scientists and pesticide victims fear an EU rollback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a970ae95552bb6347cc80106baa149ce4a8532953a80650891839829e25a1c09</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T07:10:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-so-safe-you-could-drink-it-scientists-and-pesticide-victims-fear-an-eu-rollback--79f5867b4455.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-so-safe-you-could-drink-it-scientists-and-pesticide-victims-fear-an-eu-rollback" /><summary type="html">For decades, French farmers sprayed pesticides they were told were harmless. Many have since fallen ill, grappling with cancers and other diseases caused by exposure. As the EU prepares to vote on a package that would end regular safety reviews of most pesticides, victims, doctors and scientists warn it could keep harmful products on the market for longer.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italy's biggest-ever wine heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5220bf852904efa03ca1841bda048440833d56bfec70d2a2b6db3bf1b51e2e6b</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T20:08:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-italy-s-biggest-ever-wine-heist--5d4a20ca2b50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-italy-s-biggest-ever-wine-heist" /><summary type="html">A multi million euro wine heist in Italy. As thieves in Tuscany steal 30 thousand bottles of the one of the most iconic labels in the country from a warehouse of the the prized Marchesi Antinori winery as it prepared for a major export. The company said in the past few hours, they believe two vans and up to six thieves were involved. Gavin Lee speaks to France 24's correspondent in Rome, Seema Gupta.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump strikes diesel deal with Putin, reversing years of pressure on Russia over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa2df65073088a11b5aa94424f5b4ff3265d3f9239935b326781631ab8c68aa0</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T20:00:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-trump-strikes-diesel-deal-with-putin-reversing-years-of-pressure-on-russia-over-ukraine-war--81c65c075c6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-trump-strikes-diesel-deal-with-putin-reversing-years-of-pressure-on-russia-over-ukraine-war" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that Russia had agreed to immediately supply more than 300,000 tonnes of diesel to US and global markets in an effort to cut fuel prices before November's midterm elections. The move marks a stunning change of policy after the US and its allies hit Russia with waves of sanctions over its invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU's Covid recovery fund was 'absolutely a success': European Court of Auditors' Pierre Moscovici</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d0f464b6e117ae65e32b9ee04b5dccac058a6a303b3555f4be00914799df6df</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:51:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-eu-s-covid-recovery-fund-was-absolutely-a-success-european-court-of-auditors-pierre-moscovi--05c75909711a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-eu-s-covid-recovery-fund-was-absolutely-a-success-european-court-of-auditors-pierre-moscovici" /><summary type="html">2020 was an annus horribilis. Covid stalked the land. Lockdowns, curfews and social distancing were the order of the day. But there was a silver lining: European countries showed themselves to be capable of great solidarity, jointly procuring vaccines and then agreeing on a mammoth post-Covid recovery fund, the Recovery and Resilience Facility (RRF). That fund has disbursed €450 billion in grants and loans to EU member states since 2021. As the RRF enters its crucial final phase, we take stock of the situation with Pierre Moscovici, the French member of the European Court of Auditors (ECA).</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Israel a rare dissenting voice as praise pours in for Nobel Peace Prize winner Navi Pillay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c270715b7df3a7aa263465e9ceed4c742e0c6d3e283a652aeb0dd0a8f98a50c3</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:20:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-israel-a-rare-dissenting-voice-as-praise-pours-in-for-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay--0ac82efe71b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-israel-a-rare-dissenting-voice-as-praise-pours-in-for-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay" /><summary type="html">Advocates of human rights and international justice cheered, even as Israeli officials fumed, after South African jurist and former UN human rights chief Navi Pillay won the Nobel Peace Prize on Friday. The 85-year-old drew wide praise for decades of work, including investigating crimes in Rwanda, Israel and the occupied Palestinian territories.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>International Criminal Court faces 'test of resilience' as US imposes sweeping sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef8d3937c91f706388511ccd2a945a61dee7ced6101bad0bee445c281f6bfd2e</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:19:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-international-criminal-court-faces-test-of-resilience-as-us-imposes-sweeping-sanctions--8a8a0bb4e4e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-international-criminal-court-faces-test-of-resilience-as-us-imposes-sweeping-sanctions" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has imposed sweeping new sanctions on the International Criminal Court as part of its campaign to dismantle what it describes as a "rogue" tribunal, threatening to cripple its operations. Following the move, ⁠the European Union said it was "ready to take any necessary measures to enable the court to carry out its work".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Falling test scores in schools startle EU countries: Why are standards going down?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:634661b08970886b6aba417c2e55ea16a80632c1397777f9bba8e16ccafa8537</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:03:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-falling-test-scores-in-schools-startle-eu-countries-why-are-standards-going-down--52f4dba6ca3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-falling-test-scores-in-schools-startle-eu-countries-why-are-standards-going-down" /><summary type="html">It has been dubbed "the PISA shock". Countries that had been used to their school pupils performing well in test scores are seeing a plunge in standards. The PISA test is an international assessment led by the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), which measures how well 15‑year‑olds in over 80 countries apply reading, mathematics and science skills to real‑world problems. In the latest rankings, France's results were the worst it has ever had, and Germany's school pupils got their worst PISA report card too.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Lawsuits blame Fox News for deaths of journalists in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd02763a47284cf5a3e879ebf9ef554e114fb82b07d74e0c0272b2510581f1f5</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:23:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261009-lawsuits-blame-fox-news-for-deaths-of-journalists-in-ukraine--d976749efeb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261009-lawsuits-blame-fox-news-for-deaths-of-journalists-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop revisits a fatal assignment for a Fox News team in Ukraine. On March 14, 2022, a Russian strike hit the crew reporting near the capital Kyiv. Reporter Benjamin Hall was seriously injured and two other journalists were killed. The journalists' families are suing Fox, saying the network put the story ahead of its people. Our guest is NPR's David Folkenflik.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>Residents of Ukraine's Kramatorsk forced to flee as drone strikes intensify</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23892e6ef6a3a5773f01166a02d1e163e7b6f87b202d1c4fb36fd3dd077e1288</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:51:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261009-residents-of-ukraine-s-kramatorsk-forced-to-flee-as-drone-strikes-intensify--e61c82973422.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261009-residents-of-ukraine-s-kramatorsk-forced-to-flee-as-drone-strikes-intensify" /><summary type="html">The city of Kramatorsk, in eastern Ukraine, is increasingly coming under Russian attack. For those who have stayed behind, the threat from drones and shelling has become a daily reality. Many have resisted leaving their homes, despite the growing danger – but now, more and more residents are being forced to flee. Our colleagues at France 2 followed an evacuation from the city and witnessed first-hand the dangers that residents face.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa's Navi Pillay wins 2026 Nobel Peace Prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3646f16f1e29c417b475a8004d3cc25a72cf94cf2835f2e4c0318b65955ad7da</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T09:03:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-south-africa-s-navanethem-navi-pillay-wins-2026-nobel-peace-prize--977edf946bc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-south-africa-s-navanethem-navi-pillay-wins-2026-nobel-peace-prize" /><summary type="html">Former UN human rights chief and International Court of Justice judge Navanethem "Navi" Pillay has won the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize for her contributions to international law, the Nobel jury announced on Friday. The Nobel committee denied it was taking a stance on whether Israel is committing genocide in Gaza by awarding Pillay, who led a UN inquiry on the subject, after Israel said honouring her legitimised "anti-Israel hatred".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French student protests: Police impunity ‘below' the standards of a 'well-functioning democracy’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ce6459814b2a7715d6e0e4d4c3eb5397b80ac360d4e8374bf1d2fdb142df107</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T06:55:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-french-student-protests-police-impunity-below-the-standards-of-a-well-functioning-democracy--b640f2882efb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-french-student-protests-police-impunity-below-the-standards-of-a-well-functioning-democracy-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye welcomes Dr. Antoine Marie, postdoctoral researcher, fellow and lecturer at Sciences Po / CEVIPOF, to explore the political psychology behind France’s student protests. Why do people witness the same events yet reach radically different conclusions about violence? Dr Marie examines how media echo chambers, partisan thinking and the politicization of empathy deepen polarization, making it easier to overlook the suffering of those perceived as political opponents. He also examines France’s increasingly offensive police doctrine, questions surrounding accountability, and the institutional incentives that may actually hinder independent investigations into police misconduct.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands march in Madrid to mourn pensioner whose eviction sparked housing protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0671446a214e2e796bf9123d02c33470e0d764ebb5c088111d02759f5ae4c1bb</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T06:45:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-tens-of-thousands-march-in-madrid-to-mourn-pensioner-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protest--92385d3a64ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-tens-of-thousands-march-in-madrid-to-mourn-pensioner-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of protesters joined a march in Madrid Thursday to mark the death of 87-year-old retiree Maricarmen Abascal, whose eviction from her apartment in the Spanish capital in September sparked a wave of housing protests that prompted the government to call early elections.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump envoys, European officials to discuss ‘new ideas’ for Ukraine peace in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ce901149dab2a12e19acf17e0ba1983be0bd888e5ae418645b9d064a8f73499</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T21:19:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-trump-envoys-ukraine-peace-talks-miami--619d0e85a342.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-trump-envoys-ukraine-peace-talks-miami" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump’s envoys will meet Ukrainian negotiators and European officials in Miami on Friday to discuss a new proposal to end Russia’s war in Ukraine. Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner will present ideas developed during recent talks with both sides, one source said Thursday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Black Sea and black ops: How exposed is Europe to Ukraine war spillover?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60c51bcc3ba01dd796fb56d997c6030f0051c012b3e25254c58b63d42375aeeb</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:42:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261008-black-sea-and-black-ops-how-exposed-is-europe-to-ukraine-war-spillover--b0bb3b79e51f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261008-black-sea-and-black-ops-how-exposed-is-europe-to-ukraine-war-spillover" /><summary type="html">The story is as underreported as it is consequential for the entire planet. Three Turkish-owned cargo ships out of Ukraine have been hit in EU waters by suspected Russian drones. One, the Togo-flagged Alfa Watan, sunk on Tuesday off Bulgaria. Ten Egyptian and Syrian crew members are missing. For its part, Ukraine has been hitting Russian tankers in the Black Sea, with no sign of a return to a UN-brokered deal to allow oil, grain and fertiliser ships to pass.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Spain mourns Maricarmen Abascal, whose eviction sparked housing protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df77f190fd2b8bd4983f5b4d91a1821f2e57b0bb17b2397898bc5543af37ceb3</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:35:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-mourns-maricarmen-abascal-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests--91508a8d7343.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-mourns-maricarmen-abascal-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests" /><summary type="html">Protests and anger have grown across Spain after the death of an 87-year-old woman in the wake of her eviction from her home. Maricarmen Abascal was thrown out of her home of seven decades in what became the "cause celebre" of Spain's housing crisis. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two Latvian men arrested at UK base housing US and NATO intelligence hubs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0dd765b0989005406894e183c9514490636b417e380f9c47a99281a4b14dd7f</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:57:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-two-latvian-men-arrested-at-uk-base-housing-us-and-nato-intelligence-hubs--393dadf82f17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-two-latvian-men-arrested-at-uk-base-housing-us-and-nato-intelligence-hubs" /><summary type="html">British ​counter-terrorism police are investigating after two Latvian men were arrested Thursday near a Royal Air Force ​base in southeast England housing US and NATO intelligence operations, police said in a statement. The arrests come days after a major incident at another UK base led the US military to withdraw B-1 bombers stationed there.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French, US and Russian astronauts return to Earth after eight months in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b81be6e977f6696b16bee2e1e479babb9be4c4a193e4a87dffd695215ce8416</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:02:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-french-us-and-russian-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space--ded2d2b5229c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-french-us-and-russian-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space" /><summary type="html">SpaceX brought France's Sophie Adenot and fellow astronauts Jessica Meir, Jack Hathaway and Andrey Fedyaev back to Earth on Thursday after an eight-month mission on board the International Space Station that saw Adenot become the first French woman to walk in space.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Search warrants for former prince Andrew's homes were unlawful, UK court rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e04a7c6781fe725cc83a7a48f7165da351b2136948064572a401b8efee6a5f3</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:09:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-search-warrants-for-former-prince-andrew-homes-were-unlawful-uk-court-rules--df9bf5d6c48d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-search-warrants-for-former-prince-andrew-homes-were-unlawful-uk-court-rules" /><summary type="html">Police who searched the properties of Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor as part of investigations into his links to the late sex offender Jeffrey Epstein have agreed the search warrants were unlawful, a London judge said Thursday. The 66-year-old younger brother of King Charles II was arrested on February 19 on suspicion of misconduct in public office.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>New Paris exhibition explores Ireland's housing crisis through contemporary art</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b95aec670711f2eeeac799836416f20f3f7d90eb4bd75a645ddd5e3d58435e36</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:29:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art--34e2c2f9b707.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art" /><summary type="html">Huge demonstrations have been held over the last few weeks in Spain over its housing crisis, but the issue is not restricted to Spain. Many other countries also have a huge problem with housing, including Ireland, with experts saying that for every street of 10 houses, the country actually needs 12. Now a new exhibition in Paris at the Irish Cultural Centre is trying to reflect the issue. In Perspective, we spoke to the museum's director and one of the artists taking part.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Maricarmen, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction shook Spain, dies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b9813f433f3210d09d9372e8c9068b9ec2ca5ee9ac60a45d359bcf4cff3b305</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:54:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-maricarmen-the-87-year-old-woman-whose-eviction-shook-spain-dies--c9a94189bc69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-maricarmen-the-87-year-old-woman-whose-eviction-shook-spain-dies" /><summary type="html">María del Carmen Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction from her longtime Madrid home sparked nationwide protests across Spain and unleashed a political crisis, died on Wednesday while hospitalised.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in Literature awarded to Canada’s Anne Carson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92ca21bad1ad46cd0589c0f1f4065ff06482663ef28ac34d6b99708d87aee506</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:04:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-nobel-prize-in-literature-awarded-to-canada-anne-carson--e2bf3cfdb309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-nobel-prize-in-literature-awarded-to-canada-anne-carson" /><summary type="html">The Nobel Prize in Literature was awarded to Canadian poet and essayist Anne Carson on Thursday by the Swedish Academy in Stockholm. Toronto-born Carson, 76, draws from ancient Greek and Roman literature for her works blending elements of poetry, essay and fiction. She will receive 12 million Swedish kronor (about $1.2 million) alongside the prestigious award.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Evicted pensioner Maricarmen, symbol of Spain's housing crisis, dies at 87</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdf87031bc6678da20fae7c92be99f651c0073b96071138aebd5a04f1e8d7470</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:35:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261008-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-symbol-of-spain-s-housing-crisis-dies-at-87--2674a49e3c93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261008-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-symbol-of-spain-s-housing-crisis-dies-at-87" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 8: Maricarmen, the evicted Spanish pensioner who became the face of Spain's housing crisis, dies in hospital. Also, France braces for "Act Four" of high school student protests against dilapidated schools and poor staff presence. Finally, actress Zendaya sparks a row over etiquette at Paris Fashion Week.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry></feed>
